# A package's generic forwards its type parameter into `llm.call<T>`: the
# script names the type, so the descriptor the script builds carries that
# type's schema and predicate across the package boundary, and the package
# never sees `Label`. One prompt fits the type, the other is prose.
# name          dir       deps           root
@test/triage    triage    -
main            app       @test/triage   root
